# [6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.2-alpha] - 2026-09-21\n\n### Fixed\n- [DE] **The Artists screen is no longer empty.** It opens a *library* page (`FEmusic_library_corpus_artists`), which carries the `gridRenderer` / `musicShelfRenderer` shape that `YouTube.library` maps; the screen was going through `YouTube.browse`, which only reads the two-row cards of a browse page, so the request succeeded and returned nothing — no error, no log line, blank screen (the same for the \"See all\" link in the Library feed). It now uses the library parser, the one the Library screen already uses, and every browse outcome is recorded in `browse.log` (`browse ok … → N section(s), M item(s)` / `(empty page)`), so an exported log tells an empty server page apart from a parse miss.\n\n### Commits\n- v6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.2: load the Artists screen through the library parser\n---\nThis release was built automatically from commit `eee6733eee515922d5a7a7c188ca5126dafd2e5b`.\n"},{"tag_name":"6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha","name":"Vivi Music 6.0.6.5_DE 1.53.1","published_at":"2026-09-21T17:05:50Z","prerelease":true,"draft":false,"html_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/tag/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha","assets":[{"name":"innosetup.log","size":49091,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/innosetup.log"},{"name":"INSTALL-GUIDE.md","size":10167,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/INSTALL-GUIDE.md"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-arm64.dmg","size":153124973,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-arm64.dmg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-arm64.pkg","size":147964046,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-arm64.pkg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-AUR.tar.gz","size":1528,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-AUR.tar.gz"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-setup.exe","size":130668481,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-setup.exe"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-x64.dmg","size":157032075,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-x64.dmg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-x64.pkg","size":151600916,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-x64.pkg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.AppImage","size":153876984,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.AppImage"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.deb","size":145484494,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.deb"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.msi","size":143368368,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.msi"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.rpm","size":157493576,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1.rpm"}],"body":"## Vivi Music 6.0.6.5_DE 1.53.1\n**Release channel:** `alpha`\n\n## [6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1-alpha] - 2026-09-21\n\n### Added\n- [DE] **A new lyrics style, `Alpha`.** It draws the lyrics the way the desktop did before the mobile look was ported (one plain line per lyric, the sung one in the accent colour), so the old behaviour is still one click away in the picker. Its label is translated in all 49 languages (`desktop_extra_translations_71.py`).\n\n### Fixed\n- [DE] **Every animation style now follows the mobile recipe of the same name.** `Simple`, `Fade`, `Glow`, `Slide`, `Karaoke` and `Apple Music` reuse the exact alphas, weights and halo strengths of the mobile renderer (mobile's `Glow` is a word-level halo that grows with the square of the fill — 1.53.0 had turned it into a sweep across the line, which is not what the mobile style does), `Apple Music V2` lays the line out word by word and reveals it character by character (estimating the word timings from the character counts when the source carries none), `VIVI Music` runs one global wave over the sentence with the per-word halo, the 0.75/0.50/0.30/0.20 alpha falloff, the progressive blur and the 1.05 active-line scale of the mobile style, `Lyrics V2 (Fluid)` floats each word by up to 4 dp while its bright copy is revealed behind a travelling edge, and `MetroLyrics` draws the per-word flat fill with a landing wobble and the mobile distance falloff. The whole renderer is driven by one speed-scaled timeline, so the `Animation speed` option reaches every style uniformly.\n- [DE] **The expressive player's lyrics ignored the lyrics options.** They were handed only the display object while the size and line spacing parameters defaulted to 18 sp / 1.35 and then *overrode* it, so the user's size and spacing never reached that player; it also always requested synced lyrics even with the option off. It now keeps the values the display object carries and honours the `Synced lyrics` setting.\n\n### Commits\n- v6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.1: make every lyrics style the mobile one, add Alpha\n---\nThis release was built automatically from commit `6d023d326bd58aa4fd4f3bbf15e6e158f923fad5`.\n"},{"tag_name":"6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha","name":"Vivi Music 6.0.6.5_DE 1.53.0","published_at":"2026-09-21T16:21:28Z","prerelease":true,"draft":false,"html_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/tag/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha","assets":[{"name":"innosetup.log","size":49091,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/innosetup.log"},{"name":"INSTALL-GUIDE.md","size":10167,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/INSTALL-GUIDE.md"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-arm64.dmg","size":153161205,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-arm64.dmg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-arm64.pkg","size":147947955,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-arm64.pkg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-AUR.tar.gz","size":1529,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-AUR.tar.gz"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-setup.exe","size":130654163,"download_count":1,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-setup.exe"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-x64.dmg","size":156995486,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-x64.dmg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-x64.pkg","size":151591138,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-x64.pkg"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.AppImage","size":153864696,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.AppImage"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.deb","size":145398800,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.deb"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.msi","size":143356080,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.msi"},{"name":"VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.rpm","size":157480437,"download_count":0,"browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PiBOH/vivi-music-de/releases/download/6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha/VIVIMusic-6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0.rpm"}],"body":"## Vivi Music 6.0.6.5_DE 1.53.0\n**Release channel:** `alpha`\n\n## [6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0-alpha] - 2026-09-21\n\n### Added\n- [DE] **Two more lyrics styles, so the picker matches the mobile one.** `Lyrics V2 (Fluid)` lays the sung word out as its own composable, floats it up (a sine over its own progress) and reveals its bright copy behind an edge that travels across the word instead of just recolouring it; `MetroLyrics` also animates lines whose source carries no word timings — it estimates them the way the mobile style does (180 ms per word, 30 ms apart) — and fades the rest of the list by distance from the sung line (20 / 15 / 10 / 8 %).\n\n### Changed\n- [DE] **Every lyrics style is now a style of its own.** `Glow` is a *line* effect (a light sweeps the whole line over its own duration while a halo breathes around it) instead of a slightly larger shadow on the per-word fill; `Apple Music V2` reveals the line *character by character* (the mobile granularity) instead of being the same word-level effect as `Apple Music`; `Slide` (tight leading edge, breathing halo, glow on the words already sung), `Karaoke` (wider seven-stop fill whose halo grows with the square of the progress) and `Metro` (flat, bold karaoke fill) each follow their own mobile recipe. `Animation speed` now scales all of them, including the sweep of `Glow` and the character split of `Apple Music V2`, which were the two that ignored it.\n- [DE] **Settings are grouped and ordered like the mobile app's.** The root screen went from seven groups to the mobile app's four — account and updates, media & player experience, features & data, system & support — with the mobile row order inside each (`Updates` and `Account` first, `AI translation` → `Privacy` → `Storage` → `Data saver`, `Backup & restore` → `About`); the desktop-only rows keep their place next to the mobile row they belong to (the `Lyrics` screen sits beside `Appearance`, which is where the mobile app keeps those options, and `Language` beside `Content`). `Player & audio` follows the mobile grouping too: `Audio quality` first, then a `Crossfade` group with its duration, then history duration and the playback group, then the misc group with the volume/media-key rows, and only then the desktop-only slider style and stream cache. The lyrics sub-screen uses the mobile order (position, style, glow, blur, size, spacing, tap-to-seek, auto-scroll).\n\n### Fixed\n- [DE] **`Apple Music blur` is offered only where it does anything.** The mobile app shows that option just for the VIVI Music style, and the renderer only applies it there; the desktop offered it for every style (where it silently dimmed the lines) — the row now appears for VIVI Music only and the renderer ignores a leftover value on any other style. `Animation speed` is likewise hidden while the master `Animations` switch is off, since it is a derivative of it.\n\n### Commits\n- v6.0.6.5_DE-1.53.0: give every lyrics style its own look and regroup the settings like mobile\n---\nThis release was built automatically from commit `89b883d394295697f76a19c121b40188c17713cf`.\n"},{"tag_name":"6.0.6.5_DE-1.52.9-alpha","name":"Vivi Music 6.0.6.5_DE 1.52.9","published_at